    "result_text": "All 258 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment on owner creation, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to a `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Database schemas** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). The active test profile (`hsqldb`) runs with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema DDL is what actually creates the column.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it on `GET`/`POST` responses. MapStruct auto-maps it entity\u2192DTO.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"customerCode\", ignore = true)` on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` since it's a server-assigned field, not a request input.\n\n5. **New pipeline step** `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 takes the built `@Val Owner` and `OwnerRepository`, computes `LAST3` (upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`) and `NNNN` (`findAll().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits), and sets it in place.\n\n6. **POST pipeline** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 wired `assignCustomerCode` between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance, so the sequence is computed against already-persisted owners and the code is saved.\n\nThe acceptance test (`SMI-...`/`JON-...` with a global sequence that increments by exactly 1 between consecutive creates) passes, along with the full 258-test suite.",
